+\begin{proof}
+Taylor's theorem in the Banach space of bounded operators gives
+\[
+P_\alpha(t+h)
+=
+P_\alpha(t)+h\dot P_\alpha(t)+E_{\alpha}(t,h),
+\qquad
+\|E_{\alpha}(t,h)\|\le C_1h^2,
+\]
+uniformly in $t$ and $\alpha$.  Hence
+\[
+S(\Pcal(t+h),\Pcal(t))
+=
+I+hK(t)+E(t,h),
+\qquad
+\|E(t,h)\|\le C_2h^2.
+\]
+Since $K(t)^*=-K(t)$,
+\[
+S^*S=I+E_2(t,h),
+\qquad
+\|E_2(t,h)\|\le C_3h^2.
